		(uuid "311f3d9c-38f8-5b10-81b3-33cd188acf25")
	)
	(text "SPDIF INPUT -- what is left after F26 deleted the AK4118A AND the WM8804.\nS/PDIF RX is ON-DIE in the ADAU1466 (pin 4 SPDIFIN), routed to an internal ASRC, and it\nconsumes NO serial port. So this whole sheet is a front end: terminate, isolate, couple.\n\n*** THE AC COUPLING CAPACITOR IS REQUIRED BY THE DATASHEET, NOT A PRECAUTION. *** T1-44:\nthe RX input is a comparator centred at IOVDD/2 and 'requires an AC coupling capacitor\non the pin'. Removing it does not degrade the link -- IT BREAKS THE BIAS POINT. Treat\nthis part as [HARD]: it is not a coupling cap that could be a 0R in a pinch.\n\n75 Ohm termination across the transformer primary, matched to the coax S/PDIF standard.\nCOMPARATOR MARGIN: T1-44 requires >= 200 mV p-p at the pin. Consumer S/PDIF sources\ndeliver 0.5 V p-p nominal into 75 Ohm; a 1:1 transformer passes that, so the margin is\n~2.5x at nominal. The transformer is the reason the margin is checked at all -- turns\nratio and insertion loss both live in the PN, which is why it is PINNED and not left as\na generic symbol: PE-65612NL class, 1:1, S/PDIF-rated. F38 line, F38a manufacturer axis.\n\nGALVANIC ISOLATION IS THE POINT, not impedance matching -- a source with its own mains\nground would otherwise inject a ground loop straight into the analog reference. The\nshield goes to the CHASSIS RC (S6.3), NOT to signal ground.\n\n*** SPDIF TX IS DELETED DELIBERATELY, NOT FORGOTTEN. *** The ADAU1466 has an on-die\ntransmitter (pin 5) and it costs nothing to leave enabled in firmware, but NO\nrequirement in S1 or S12 asks for a digital output, and a DNP jack would spend panel\narea on an outline that is still Block D UNSET. SPDIF_TX_OUT lands on a TESTPOINT so\nthe capability stays reachable for bring-up. Reopen if an output is ever specified --\nthe silicon is already paid for."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 359.41 39.37 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "1743df77-c47d-5931-902b-5fe749fef8c9")
	)
